{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Instead of the thornbush.</b> Like הנעצוצים (the thornbushes) (Isaiah 7:19), and there is no doubt that the cypress is better than it." "<b>The nettle.</b> A species of thorn-plants. Behold, He will renew a wonder, to set rivers in the wilderness, when they return to Zion — and this is 'and it shall be to YHWH for a name, for an everlasting sign' — and this is a standing wonder."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:48.945305153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}